      "content": "that's a really powerful way to put it—the \"social languages\" thing is a perfect concept for the show's themes.\n\ni want to dig into that part about how liam might misinterpret their vigilance as \"aggression\" or \"instability.\" for the script, i need to understand if this is just a misunderstanding, or if there's an underlying, almost subconscious truth to his perception. \n\nfrom a writer's standpoint, i want to know: when liam looks at someone like keoni, does his instinct tell him he's looking at someone \"unpredictable\" or \"volatile\" simply because of how they carry themselves? and on the flip side, when the street-smart characters look at liam's \"strategic advantage,\" do they see it as something purely earned through intelligence, or do they instinctively view it as just the product of a system that was rigged in his favor from the start? \n\nbasically, i'm trying to see if their very presence feels \"correct\" or \"incorrect\" to the other based purely on their social standing.",
