      "content": "interesting. you're touching on some really heavy stuff regarding \"hollow\" accomplishments versus \"genuine\" worlds.\n\nto help the actors prepare for these conflicting perspectives, i want to look at the \"inherent\" nature of these traits. when you say their experiences make them \"unpredictable\" or \"volatile\" to liam, or that their world is more \"genuine\" than his, it suggests there's an almost biological or fundamental difference in how they move through the world.\n\ncan u expand on that? specifically, does the \"street-smart\" character's need for vigilance actually change their core temperament—making them more \"instinctual\" or \"reactive\" by nature? and in contrast, does liam's environment cultivate a temperament that is more \"cerebral\" or \"detached\"? \n\ni want to see if we can articulate whether these aren't just learned behaviors, but if their backgrounds actually create these different \"natural\" states of being.",
